--- body ---

## Context

Deliver one representative project and a small shared candidate set before broad migration. Reuse existing content; do not combine the pilot with corpus-wide English rewriting or quality annotation.

Design baseline: v7. v6 was merged by PR #903 and is frozen at `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design-v6.md`; v7 closes the acceptance review's four §12.1 conditions and settles the nomenclature, leaving the architecture and this ticket's scope unchanged. See `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design.md`, `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design-nomenclature.md` and `docs/2026-09-11-memory-implementation-plan.md`. This planning change implements nothing and closes no work.

## Relevant files

Baseline/mapping from 0917; legacy import from 0908; schema/admission package; one chosen project repository; IDH project and shared memory roots.

## Actions

1. Select and document a representative pilot and corpus revision; separate IDH project memory from shared knowledge. **This ticket owns the v7 §12.1 disjoint-roots row.** IDH's repository *is* the runtime's home (`README` lines 7 and 77), so the store cannot leave `~/.claude`; what moves is its position relative to the runtime's *declared* native root, which today is `~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/` (`provenance.py` `PROJECTS_BASE`). Perform both moves inside the harness repository — `memory/` → `memory-shared/`, and `projects/-home-haduong--claude/memory/` → `memory/` — and repoint every existing reader that hard-codes the old paths (`HARNESS_MEMORY` in `skills/dream/provenance.py`, `skills/dream/read-index.py`, the resident census).
2. Assign UUIDs once and preserve a durable old-path-to-UUID mapping; migrate explicit lifecycle, scope, dates and relative navigation. Preserve source text unless a separately reviewed correction is necessary.
3. Fix a bounded available shared candidate set before ranking. Commit readable replicas with UUID, source revision and hash; never copy credentials or private traces indiscriminately.
4. Implement reusable bounded snapshot selection/refresh for every publication, invoked by dreaming and consumed by 0910. Include referenced shared bodies plus the bounded candidate selection; resolve dependencies or report them unavailable. Reconcile live/shared replicas by UUID and proven revision ancestry: accept verified successors, report divergence, never use timestamps as winners. Retain source revisions/refresh date, validate hashes and propagate known withdrawals even when replacement bodies are outside the set. Refreshed successors remain recent until explicitly processed. Treat uncached sources as unavailable, not refill candidates; document offline staleness. Replicas are not independently editable; propose changes upstream or create a distinct local observation.
5. Provide catalogue input fixtures, inactive navigation and rollback instructions. Report language exceptions and unavailable evidence for later reviewed treatment.

## Test

Relocate a fresh pilot clone without the originating home directory. Verify plain Markdown navigation, inactive notices, identity-preserving replicas, verified-successor versus divergent refresh, missing referenced dependencies, retained particulars and idempotent rerun without new UUIDs. Refresh a stale shared replica after an upstream withdrawal with an uncached replacement: the withdrawal survives export and is present in the committed snapshot and manifest after refresh, with the uncached replacement reported unavailable; offline readers explicitly cannot know unseen upstream changes. Whether that withdrawal is *effective at the next supported load* is 0921's test, not this one — there is no loader at this position.

## Verification

- [ ] Run the focused fixtures and show they detect the relevant failure.
- [ ] Run applicable repository checks; record commands, results and limitations.
- [ ] Confirm the implementation matches this scope and v7, including explicit capability limits.

## Invariants

- Canonical bodies and provenance remain reviewable; memory cannot override decisions.
- No mandatory residency, automatic generalisation, new native-memory modes or policy duplication.
- Use the common library and normal Git integration; no runtime implementation is part of the planning PR.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] One portable project and shared snapshot can be read offline without harness installation.
- [ ] No automatic generalisation or loss of local conditions.
- [ ] All migrated bodies reconcile to baseline identities; no broad rollout hidden in the pilot.
- [ ] The v7 §12.1 disjoint-roots fixture passes against the adapter's declared native root, so 0923 can record the row green rather than known red. Until then the row stays red with its reason; it is this ticket that clears it, not 0913.
